language 0.1.0
module interaction
  means
    Purposeful interaction of actors with a system: their goals, use cases,
    scenarios, inputs and observable outcomes, independent of any particular
    interface.

entity actor : thing
  means
    actor: a subject or external system taking part in a scenario of
    interaction in a definite role.

entity goal : thing
  means
    goal: the desired outcome for the sake of which an actor begins an
    interaction.

entity use-case : thing
  means
    use case: a description of a complete interaction by which an actor
    reaches a goal.

entity scenario : thing
  means
    scenario: one admissible sequence of steps of a use case.

entity step : thing
  means
    step: a single action of an actor or of the system, indivisible from the
    point of view of the scenario.

entity input : thing
  means
    input: information or influence required for a step to be performed.

entity outcome : thing
  means
    outcome: an observable state or value arising from the performance of a
    step or a scenario.
